---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Hero from '../../components/Hero.astro';
import Prose from '../../components/Prose.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  locale="en"
  title="About — Luvita"
  description="Luvita is a software company based in Bodrum, Türkiye. We build custom software for enterprise clients and ship products of our own."
  paths={{ tr: 'hakkimizda', en: 'about' }}
>
  <Hero
    eyebrow="About"
    title="We treat software as a craft"
    lead="We are a software company based in Bodrum, Türkiye — building software designed to last, and maintained like it matters."
  />

  <section class="container">
    <Prose>
      <p>
        Luvita is a technology company based in Bodrum, Muğla, building custom
        software for enterprise clients. We work with the rigor that banking
        and enterprise workflows demand: architecture decisions are
        documented, testing and automation are set up from day one, and every
        system we deliver stays under our care.
      </p>
      <p>
        Our founder, <strong>Mert Yılmaz Ertuğrul</strong>, brings years of
        engineering experience in banking and enterprise software. Java/Spring
        Boot backend systems, cross-platform applications with Flutter, and
        cloud architectures are the company's core competencies.
      </p>
      <p>
        Alongside client work, we build our own products:
        <strong>SliceFocus</strong> and <strong>LexiPower</strong> are live on
        the App Store. Taking software from idea to store and keeping it alive
        for years is the quality bar we bring to every engagement.
      </p>
      <h2>Our principles</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Transparency:</strong> scope, timeline and risks are shared
          openly at every stage.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Longevity:</strong> code is written for the team that reads
          it years later; docs and tests are first-class deliverables.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Ownership:</strong> delivery is not an ending — it is the
          start of a long-term partnership.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </Prose>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
